{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-core":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-core/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-glossary-monoidal-category","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Remark","doco:Section"],"label":"rem:glossary-monoidal-category","kind":"remark","title":"Monoidal category","tags":["glossary","category-theory","monoidal"],"defines":["monoidal-category"],"text":"glossary-monoidal-category.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"rem:glossary-monoidal-category\"></a><p><strong><dfn class=\"defterm\" id=\"term-monoidal-category\">Monoidal category</dfn>.</strong> A category <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbf{C}</code> equipped with a bifunctor <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\otimes \\colon \\mathbf{C} \\times \\mathbf{C} \\to \\mathbf{C}</code>, a distinguished unit object <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbf{1}</code>, and coherent natural isomorphisms for associativity (<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\alpha</code>), left unitality (<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\lambda</code>), and right unitality (<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\rho</code>). These satisfy Mac Lane's pentagon and triangle axioms.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/notation/glossary-monoidal-category.md","heading":"Remark","number":"30.2.2","page":"b/rem-glossary-monoidal-category","qa":{"counts":{"pass":60,"fail":0,"warn":0,"na":17,"unknown":0,"stale":60},"milnor":{"total":2,"notPassing":0}}}
